@startuml 1-overview
!include style.iuml
title 1. Overview - who talks to whom

allowmixing
hide members
hide circle

package "view (boundary)" {
  interface GameView BOUNDARY
  class ConsoleView BOUNDARY
  class SwingView <<extra>> BOUNDARY
}

package "controller (control)" {
  class GameController CONTROL
  class GameConfig CONTROL
  class GameResult CONTROL
}

package "staff" {
  abstract class Staff STAFF
  class Host STAFF
  class Waiter STAFF
  class Chef STAFF
  class Cashier STAFF
}

package "model (domain)" {
  class Restaurant DOMAIN
  class Table DOMAIN
  abstract class Customer DOMAIN
  class Order DOMAIN
}

package "menu & pricing" {
  class Menu MENU
  class MenuItem MENU
  class PriceCalculator MENU
  class HappyHour MENU
}

actor Manager

Manager -down-> GameView : choices
GameView <|.. ConsoleView
GameView <|.. SwingView

GameController -up-> GameView : asks for choices,\nshows state
GameController --> GameConfig : base setting
GameController ..> GameResult : judges the end
GameController *-- Restaurant
GameController *-- Staff : 4 staff
GameController *-- Menu
GameController *-- HappyHour

Staff <|-- Host
Staff <|-- Waiter
Staff <|-- Chef
Staff <|-- Cashier
Staff ..> Restaurant : acts on

Restaurant *-- "2" Table
Restaurant o-- "0..6" Customer
Table -- "0..1" Customer : occupant
Customer -- "0..1" Order
Order --> "1" MenuItem
Menu o-- "6" MenuItem
Waiter --> PriceCalculator : prices orders
PriceCalculator --> HappyHour

legend right
  <b>How to read this set</b>
  This page shows only the classes and how they connect.
  Diagrams 2-5 zoom into each area with attributes,
  operations, visibility and multiplicities.

  <back:#E3F2FD> boundary </back> user interface
  <back:#FFF3E0> control </back> runs the turns
  <back:#F3E5F5> staff </back> one task per turn
  <back:#E8F5E9> domain </back> game state and rules
  <back:#FFFDE7> menu & pricing </back>

  Rules never live in the view: the view only
  collects choices; staff and domain objects
  decide whether a choice is allowed.
endlegend
@enduml
